{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memcachedcache", "label": "MemcachedCache", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Right when you already run Memcached or need a pure cache: simpler protocol, smaller footprint, zero persistence. mget/mset are parallelised single-key operations because Memcached has no multi-key commands."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_server_side_lru", "label": "Server-side LRU eviction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The decision is made in the server and the client is not consulted, so there is no equivalent of InMemoryCache's guarantee-aware ordering: an entry written by setIfAbsent can disappear with most of its TTL left and nothing in the API reports it. Needs only memory pressure, unlike the topology hazard."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_add_atomicity", "label": "ADD is atomic per server, not per cluster", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ADD is atomic on the one server a key hashes to, which makes setIfAbsent correct in steady state; a topology change rehashes the keyspace, the key can land on a server with no entry, and the lock is handed out twice. There is no client-side fix without reaching into memjs's internal hashring, so keep the server list fixed for a lock's lifetime or use a fencing token; Redis is the better locking backend."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memjs_peer", "label": "memjs peer dependency", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "memjs supplies SASL auth, hash-distribution across servers and its own connection pool, which the framework does not manage directly."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memcachedcache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memcachedcache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_server_side_lru", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memcachedcache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_add_atomicity", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memcachedcache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_memjs_peer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_server_side_lru", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_guarantee_carrying_entries", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/memcached.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_memcached_add_atomicity", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_set_if_absent", "relatio